## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | flutter_app/lib/ui/widgets/file_browser.dart | 🚨 blocking the mounted session fix stops at the mount root — file opens and uploads inside mounted subfolders still fail the gh 2131 symptom probe verified on this head envpath prefixes subdirectory segments with the mount namespace but childpath s non empty segments branch does not dart string childpath string name if segments isempty return navigatesmountnamespace projectmountsegment name name return segments join name ← bare even at a live mount at a live mount with no cwd override envcwdresolvestomountsegment true projectmountenv map only rewrites project… paths a bare src nested txt falls through to the container delegate which resolves it against the app container cwd localfilesystem resolve → container src nested txt — never a real path verified with a runnable probe on this exact pr head using the same rig as test file browser test dart drill into src → listing works this pr s envpath fix ✔ tap nested txt → could not load file · no such file or directory renders the body never does widget level probe error shown true body shown false upload while inside src writeuploadbatch line 652 → writebinaryfile src name succeeds but lands in the app container not the project folder container listing src mount side empty worse than the open failure the success snackbar lies and the file is invisible in the listing so the ticket contract opening any file in a mounted session failed and the pr description fixes file opens folder drill downs and uploads hold only for the mount root and for listings the new regression tests miss it the drill down test taps the folder and asserts the listing — it never taps nested txt nor uploads from the subfolder fix one line mirrors envpath dart string childpath string name final joined segments isempty name segments join name return navigatesmountnamespace projectmountsegment joined joined and extend the regression tests open a file inside the mounted subfolder assert the body renders and upload into it assert it lands under project … not the container both fail on current head — i verified |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/network/key_wallet.dart | ⚠️ important sign out purge keys on an inferred identity — password null ⇔ account synced dart final synced networks entries where e e value password null map e e key tolist i verified the invariant holds on every current producer the join sheet refuses an empty password join sheet dart 130 132 networksessionmanager join createnetwork always record one and syncaccountnetworks inserts passwordless while preserving any stored password so today the purge is correct and the gh 2131 behavior signed out list no longer shows account networks guest joins stay is right the debt the criterion is convention only spread across four producer sites and the failure mode is destructive — one future passwordless join path e g open networks with no credential would make sign out silently delete the user s memberships and their channel keys channels removewhere key key startswith id irrecoverable from the wallet the doc comment has to argue the equivalence in prose which is the smell cheap hardening carry the fact in the data model instead of inferring it — e g a networkentry synced flag or a keywallet isaccountsynced id helper maintained at insert time so clearaccount purges exactly what syncaccountnetworks wrote not asking for a behavior change — the behavior is correct pin the invariant so the next producer can t quietly break it |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

